My friends & I were playing an RPG-ish board game over the weekend, and
a couple of times ran into situations where we had to decide which
armor was the better to keep equipped, where the answer wasn't entirely
clear, because certain armor, while weaker in general cases, gave a
benefit against certain types of monsters.  (Dragon Scale Mail--yes, it
was in there!--gave a bonus against dragons, for instance.)

This, of course, got me thinking about Nethack, and how the question
isn't "Should I wear DSM, or something else?", but simply, "Should I
wear silver or gray DSM?", with the answer often dictated by your role
(and its accompanying guaranteed equipment).  Regulars on RGRN are well
aware that periodically someone bemoans DSM's clear-cut primacy; I
guess it's my turn.

However, it occured to me that Nethack currently has some weapons that
are better against certain types of monsters than other, generally
stronger weapons (silver, for instance, and some of the more generally
useless artifact weapons); what if certain armor had a bonus against
certain types of attack damage?  (I like splitting attack damage into
various types rather than giving certain armor a bonus against certain
monsters for pretty much the same reason no one ever uses Trollbane.)
Some games break damage down into blunt, slashing, and piercing types,
for instance; padded armor is good against blunt damage, but not
slashing/piercing; platemail is weak against piercing, etc.  This would
make armor selection more complex, of course, but it would make it less
clear-cut.  I think.

It also has the benefit of giving more meaning to the difference
between "The rothe bites!" (piercing damage) and "The unicorn kicks!"
(blunt damage), so players would be encouraged to consider not just how
many attacks a monster gets, but also what sorts of attacks they are.

One big problem I can think of would be displaying the information for
the player; the best I've been able to come up with is to change the
current "AC: -15" display to B/S/P: "AC: -10/-18/-7", though that does
add still more information to the status line.

Thoughts?

